# Auto-deploy lexhub

After finishing user-facing code changes (frontend and/or backend) for Sanad / LexHub:

1. **Deploy immediately** to the VPS (`51.38.78.23`, `/opt/sanad`) — do **not** wait for the user to say "ok", "go", or "déploie".
2. Push changed files via SFTP/paramiko (same pattern as `scripts/vps_push_*.py`), then restart the relevant containers (`frontend` and/or `backend`) with:
   `docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.lexhub.yml ...`
3. Tell the user briefly that it is live on https://lexhub.space (hard refresh if needed).
4. Exception: skip deploy only for pure local docs, unfinished WIP the user said to keep local, or when SSH/credentials fail (then report the failure).
